# Git commits & PRs (GNO)

## Commits

- Only commit when the user asks (or explicitly says to push / open a PR).
- Message: short why-focused summary (1–2 sentences). Prefer imperative mood.
  - Good: `Add paginated change log with campaign filter`
  - Bad: `Update files` / `Fix stuff` / dump of file names
- Use a HEREDOC for the message body when committing via CLI.
- Never commit `.env`, keys, tokens, or local Supabase secrets.
- Never use `--no-verify` / skip hooks unless the user asks.
- Do not amend pushed commits unless the user explicitly requests it and amend rules are met.

## Pull requests

- One concern per PR when splitting is reasonable.
- Title matches the change intent; body has:
  - **Summary** — 1–3 bullets of what/why
  - **Test plan** — checklist (typecheck, tests, manual UI path)
- Push with `-u` when creating the branch remote; return the PR URL when done.
- Do not force-push `main`/`master`.

## Repos

- Each GNO tool is its **own** git repo. Do not nest both tools in one remote.
